
  finding and verifying moduli (Rabin):
    n = 15  l = 5   [0, 1]
    n = 18  l = 6   [0, 3]
    n = 21  l = 7   [0, 2]
    n = 24  l = 8   [0, 1, 3, 4]

  ── deciding one target that does NOT decompose ──────────────────
    l    n        triples  triples/gen  triples/1wd  pairs+solve   speedup
    5   15           5984       0.004s       0.000s       0.000s      4.1x
    6   18          45760       0.025s       0.003s       0.000s      8.2x
    7   21         357760       0.259s       0.028s       0.002s     18.0x
    8   24        2829056       2.191s       0.232s       0.007s     34.7x

  ── what that means for a whole run ─────────────────────────────
    l    n samples   decomp %   1/3! = %     s/target    collection      / 2^n
    5   15    4000      20.9%      16.7%      1.02e-4       1.6e-2s    4.78e-7
    6   18    4000      13.5%      16.7%      4.07e-4       1.9e-1s    7.38e-7
    7   21    4000      15.7%      16.7%      1.62e-3        1.3e0s    6.30e-7
    8   24    3065      15.0%      16.7%      6.53e-3        1.1e1s    6.62e-7

  The last column is the point.  Relation collection costs
  2^l relations x 3! tries x O(2^2l) per try = Theta(2^n),
  independent of l: a bigger factor base needs fewer tries but
  each try costs proportionally more.  Any enumeration oracle,
  however fast, sits at 2^n -- versus 2^(n/2) for Pollard rho.

